        "original_id": "cc324f32-c815-5f95-b7a8-98c3a60ab7ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Carl, Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger, Eric Forrest\n- Bands: Voivod\n- Albums: Bone Against Steel, Negatron\n- Roles: vocalist, keyboard player, singer, lyricist, bass player\n\nFacts:\n- Max Carl Gronenthal was born on January 29, 1950, and he is an American rock singer, keyboardist, guitarist, and songwriter.\n- Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger was born on August 9, 1964, and he is the vocalist and lyricist of the Canadian heavy metal band Voivod.\n- In 1994, Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger temporarily left Voivod.\n- On the album Negatron, Eric Forrest, who was Voivod's bass player, assumed vocal duties for the recording, making it the first studio album not to feature original singer Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger.\n- Bone Against Steel was the last album to feature Max Carl as vocalist and keyboard player.\n- Bone Against Steel was the band's last album until its 1996 comeback.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
